---
const steps = [
  {
    number: '01',
    title: 'Add a driver',
    body: 'Use a name or a nickname. Labels stay in your browser and are never uploaded. Turn the CDL switch off if the driver does not hold a CDL.',
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    title: 'Enter the dates you already have',
    body: 'Medical certificate issue or expiration, MVR pull, CDL expiration, annual review, road test, and employment verification. Partial dates are allowed.',
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    title: 'Read the next due date',
    body: 'Each driver gets an estimated next due date plus overdue, 30-day, and 60-day groups. The fleet summary shows the three most urgent items.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2 id="how-title">Three steps, no account</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      {steps.map((step) => (
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">{step.number}</span>
          <h3>{step.title}</h3>
          <p>{step.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="formula">
      <h3>The calculation, in plain terms</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>next due = anchor date + rule period.</strong> Dates are date-only and calculated in
        UTC, so a time zone cannot shift them by a day. Month-end dates are clamped: January 31 plus
        one month becomes February 28, or February 29 in a leap year.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the medical certificate, the expiration date you enter is always used first. If you only
        have the issue date, the tracker estimates issue date + 24 months and labels the result
        <strong>Estimated</strong>. CDL expiration is never estimated: it uses only the state-issued
        date you enter.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        Status boundaries: a date one day in the past is overdue; 0–30 days is due within 30 days;
        31–60 days is due within 60 days; 61 days or more is on track. The device date is used for
        the comparison.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .step {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 6px solid var(--manila);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }

  .step-number {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--manila-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .step p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .formula {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border-left: 6px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .formula p {
    max-width: 78ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .formula p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
